      <version name="0.6.3" author="GSS-Reaper" time="2026-11-08T21:30:25Z">
        <changelog>Fix the Talkback button: it now stays red while you hold it, reads "Talkback" and fits its column. Pressing it applies the microphone input chosen in Settings to the TALKBACK track, so talkback works without re-running Set up this session. In mix mode the Metronome row is hidden from the Cues list (the Click track in Options replaces it). In stems mode the panel shows a Metronome button (opens REAPER's metronome settings); the metronome entry is called Metronome by default, can be renamed, and has no stereo/mono type. Settings: "New tracks get" now has its label before the drop-down and its own (?) help; in stems mode a new "Replace cues with Drums, Guitars, Bass, Vocals" button gives a typical starting list. The label column is a little wider.</changelog>
